{
 "type": "FeatureCollection",
 "metadata": {
  "note": "The northern leg of the Illinois Central/Yazoo & Mississippi Valley 'Delta Route': Memphis south to Vicksburg, continuing on to Baton Rouge and New Orleans (see ymv_baton_rouge.geojson for that already-mapped southern leg -- this file's geometry connects directly to its northern endpoint at Vicksburg). The Memphis-Grenada portion has real antebellum roots: the Mississippi and Tennessee Railroad, incorporated Oct 16 1852, completed the line in 1861, connecting at Grenada to the Mississippi Central toward Jackson and, eventually, New Orleans. The Illinois Central purchased the M&T in 1886/89. The Grenada-Vicksburg portion's exact predecessor company and completion date is less clearly sourced; the whole route was consolidated into the Yazoo & Mississippi Valley subsidiary by 1892 alongside the Louisville, New Orleans and Texas Railway's Vicksburg-Baton Rouge-New Orleans line. GEOMETRY METHODOLOGY: real-traced through OpenStreetMap active-rail data (Overpass API, shortest-path graph search) -- still active Canadian National (ex-IC) freight trackage today. Traced length 357.6 km / 222.2 mi.",
  "source": "Wikipedia (Mississippi and Tennessee Railroad, Yazoo and Mississippi Valley Railroad, Grenada station), trains-and-railroads.com",
  "pulled": "20260823",
  "line_label_audit": "2026-08-24: line labels normalised repo-wide to \"<operating company>: <line name>\" -- the company's common display name (legal suffixes dropped), then the line as a passenger would have known it, or its two terminals where the line carried no advertised name. Long intermediate station lists were reduced to endpoints. For features spanning several operators the company shown is the one that ran the line for most of its drawn years. See CLAUDE.md Rule 6.",
  "rule4_audit": "2026-08-27: this layer was a single feature, coloured #8b5a2b, whose segments[] ran from the Mississippi and Tennessee Railroad (1861-1892) straight through the Yazoo & Mississippi Valley / Illinois Central years (1892-1967) - the two faults CLAUDE.md Rule 4 names at once: a company colour that disagreed with the same company elsewhere in the repo, and one feature quietly spanning an ownership change. Fixed by splitting at 1892 into two features on identical geometry and recolouring the post-1892 feature to the Illinois Central's repo-wide #F4801F. The M&T half keeps #8b5a2b, which is that company's only appearance on the map."
 },
